{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"`scripts/` (41 files) is excluded from every static gate: `Makefile:11` sets `sources = src tests`,\nso `make lint` never sees it, and `Makefile:205` runs `mypy src/rebar`, so `make typecheck` never\nsees it either. `ruff check scripts/` today reports **78 violations**.\n\nBlast radius is low — this workflow tooling is not shipped to clients — but seven of these files are\ninvoked directly by `.github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml`, the blocking workflow behind the\n`Verified` vote: `check_verify_gate_parity.py` (:130), `check_comment_hygiene.py` (:144),\n`check_raw_git_writes.py` (:162), `check_wall_clock_asserts.py` (:176), `gen_env_registry.py` (:419),\n`check_docs_index.py` (:441), `check_readme_quickstart.py` (:452). The gate implementations are\nthemselves ungated.\n\n## The 28 substantive violations\n\n| Rule | n | Nature |\n|---|---|---|\n| `RUF100` unused-noqa | 12 | Dead directives; `ruff --fix` removes them |\n| `E501` line-too-long | 11 | Rewrap; no behavior |\n| `RUF005` collection-concat | 2 | `prefix + [x]` -> `[*prefix, x]`; both in `check_complexity_baseline.py:181,187` |\n| `RUF059` unused unpack | 2 | `jira_dc_epic_link_clear_probe.py:212,222` — `b1`/`b2` captured, never read |\n| `B905` zip without `strict=` | 1 | `check_wall_clock_asserts.py:101` |\n\n**No live defect is present in this set.** Two candidates were checked and cleared:\n\n- `B905` at `check_wall_clock_asserts.py:101` is `zip(sub.ops, sub.comparators)` over an\n  `ast.Compare`. Those lists are equal-length by construction (`a < b < c` yields `ops=[Lt,Lt]`,\n  `comparators=[b,c]`), so the silent-truncation failure mode cannot occur. `strict=True` is correct\n  as hardening, not a fix.\n- The two `RUF059` sites capture an HTTP response body the probe deliberately does not inspect\n  (read-back is a separate `_req` call). `_`-prefix them.\n\nThe `RUF100` count is itself the argument for the gate: 12 `noqa` directives are dead *because*\nnothing lints the directory. Five reference rules not in `select` (`PLC0415`, `S603`, `S310`,\n`PLR0915`) — confirm none documents a live intent before deleting.\n\n## The 50 T201 (print) violations — exempt, do not fix\n\nPrint discipline in local workflow tooling is low value, and these scripts' prints are their output.\nThey sit in 10 files with no `per-file-ignores` entry: `calibrate_completion_floor.py` (11),\n`check_verify_gate_parity.py` (7), `verify_mcp_publisher_pin.py` (6), `check_raw_git_writes.py` (6),\n`t5c_calibrate.py` (5), `check_wall_clock_asserts.py` (5), `check_commit_message_wrap.py` (4),\n`check_build_env_locked.py` (3), `check_dco_identity.py` (2), `normalize_ci_conclusion.py` (1).\n\n**Resolve with ONE whole-directory entry `\"scripts/**\" = [\"T201\"]`, replacing the nine existing\nsingle-file `scripts/*.py` entries** (`pyproject.toml:461,465,468,471,475,479,483,487,491`). This\ntakes `per-file-ignores` from 17 entries to 9 and converts the scripts exemption from nine\ndiscretionary per-file entries into a single INVARIANT whole-directory one — the same shape as\n`\"tests/**\"`, which the config already marks PERMANENT. It shrinks and hardens the allowlist rather\nthan growing it. Adding ten NEW single-file entries instead is explicitly rejected.\n\n## Risk\n\nLow. 25 of the 28 are provably zero-behavior. The remaining 3 need a reviewer who reads the\nsurrounding logic rather than the diff, and `check_complexity_baseline.py` is a gate whose own\ncorrectness is being edited.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] All 12 `RUF100`, 11 `E501`, 2 `RUF005`, 2 `RUF059` and 1 `B905` violations in `scripts/` are\n      resolved\n- [x] Any deleted `noqa` referencing a non-enabled rule is confirmed to document no live intent\n- [x] The nine single-file `scripts/*.py` T201 entries are replaced by one `\"scripts/**\" = [\"T201\"]`;\n      `per-file-ignores` has FEWER entries after this change than before\n- [x] `scripts/` is added to the lint scope (`Makefile` `sources`) so `make lint` covers it, and CI\n      is green on the result\n- [x] The seven CI-invoked gate scripts behave identically: verified by a CI run, not inspection\n- [x] A follow-up ticket records the remaining `mypy` gap (`make typecheck` is `mypy src/rebar`;\n      `scripts/` and `tests/` are untyped)\n\n## CORRECTION (plan-review BLOCK, criteria G1G2/G6) — the formatter class was unbudgeted\n\nThe violation inventory above is built solely from `ruff check scripts/`. But adding `scripts`\nto the Makefile `sources` variable also enrolls all 41 files in `ruff format --check $(sources)`\n(`Makefile:153`, run by `make lint`) and `ruff format $(sources)` (`Makefile:149`).\n\nMeasured on the current tree: `ruff format --check scripts/` reports **7 files would be\nreformatted, 37 already formatted**. That is a second, entirely separate failure class from the\n78 `ruff check` findings, and `make lint` / CI would go red on it the moment `scripts` joins\n`sources`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria (supersedes the list above)\n\n- [x] The 28 substantive `ruff check` violations are resolved (RUF100 x12, E501 x11, RUF005 x2,\n      RUF059 x2, B905 x1)\n- [x] The 7 formatter-nonconforming scripts are reformatted, so `ruff format --check scripts/`\n      is clean BEFORE `scripts` is added to `sources`\n- [x] The 50 T201 (print) violations are exempted via a single consolidated `per-file-ignores`\n      entry, not 10 per-file entries\n- [x] `scripts/` is added to the Makefile `sources` variable and `make lint` is green\n- [x] The five `RUF100` directives referencing rules not in `select` (`PLC0415`, `S603`, `S310`,\n      `PLR0915`) are each confirmed not to document a live intent before deletion\n- [x] No behaviour change to any script invoked by `.github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml`\n\n\n## CORRECTION 2 (plan-review BLOCK, criterion G6) — the consolidation creates NEW RUF100\n\nAdding a single `\"scripts/**\" = [\"T201\"]` per-file-ignores entry makes every EXISTING inline\n`# noqa: T201` directive in scripts/ redundant. RUF100 (unused-noqa) is enabled, so each redundant\ndirective becomes a NEW violation.\n\nMeasured on the current tree: **28 inline `# noqa: T201` directives across 13 files**. The\n\"RUF100 x12\" figure in the inventory above was measured against the PRE-consolidation config and\ndoes not include these.\n\nThis makes the work ORDER load-bearing. The two steps cannot be done independently:\n\n1. Add the consolidated `\"scripts/**\" = [\"T201\"]` per-file-ignores entry, AND\n2. Delete all 28 now-redundant inline `# noqa: T201` directives\n\nin the SAME change, or `make lint` is red in between.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria (supersedes both lists above)\n\n- [x] The 28 substantive pre-existing `ruff check` violations are resolved (RUF100 x12, E501 x11,\n      RUF005 x2, RUF059 x2, B905 x1)\n- [x] The 7 formatter-nonconforming scripts are reformatted, so `ruff format --check scripts/` is\n      clean BEFORE `scripts` joins `sources`\n- [x] T201 is exempted via ONE consolidated `\"scripts/**\"` per-file-ignores entry, and in the SAME\n      change all 28 inline `# noqa: T201` directives are deleted, so no new RUF100 is introduced\n- [x] `scripts/` is added to the Makefile `sources` variable and `make lint` is green\n- [x] The five `RUF100` directives referencing rules not in `select` (`PLC0415`, `S603`, `S310`,\n      `PLR0915`) are each confirmed not to document a live intent before deletion\n- [x] `ruff check scripts/` and `ruff format --check scripts/` are both clean at the end\n- [x] No behaviour change to any script invoked by `.github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml`\n- [x] The post-sweep irreducible exception count is recorded on this ticket\n"}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786090553522349001,"uuid":"e4fd608a-aee4-4e1e-a380-632667421747"}